WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.320
In the fly embryo, the cells that will make the nervous system sit in small groups.

2
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.860
The cells start out equal, and every cell can become a neural precursor.

3
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.880
Yet usually only one does.

4
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.600
Something must break the tie.

5
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:28.180
First the group becomes able, and then the cells signal to each other until one wins.

6
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:30.593
Take two neighbours in the cluster.

7
00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:36.593
Proneural genes encode transcription factors that make both cells able to become

8
00:00:36.593 --> 00:00:41.113
neural. Think of it as a casting call, where everyone gets to audition.

9
00:00:42.453 --> 00:00:47.493
Proneural proteins raise their own expression, and in the textbook model they also

10
00:00:47.493 --> 00:00:51.533
raise Delta. Delta is a protein in the cell membrane.

11
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:57.927
Delta on one cell binds Notch on the cell it touches, and pulls.

12
00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.767
Two cuts then free the inner part of Notch.

13
00:01:02.547 --> 00:01:04.407
That part enters the nucleus.

14
00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:11.167
There, with a protein called CSL, it turns on the Enhancer of split genes.

15
00:01:12.047 --> 00:01:16.167
These genes encode repressors that switch proneural genes off.

16
00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:25.257
Follow the loop. More Delta on cell A means more Notch activity in cell B. Cell B

17
00:01:25.257 --> 00:01:30.357
makes more repressor, so it has less proneural activity and less Delta.

18
00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:36.097
Then cell A gets less Notch activity, and its proneural activity rises.

19
00:01:37.217 --> 00:01:40.437
The loop has closed, and cell A has pulled ahead.

20
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:47.220
Each cell inhibits its neighbour, so two inhibitions in a row make positive

21
00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:53.160
feedback. A perfectly balanced pair could sit in the middle, like a pencil on its

22
00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.480
point. But noise gives one cell slightly more Delta.

23
00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:03.180
The loop magnifies that small difference until one cell becomes the neural

24
00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:08.780
precursor. Either outcome is stable, and which cell wins is a matter of chance.

25
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:12.440
Now take Notch away from the embryo.

26
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.160
Without the receptor, no cell can be told "not you".

27
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.520
Both cells keep their proneural genes on, and both become neural.

28
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.560
In the whole embryo, that means far too many neuroblasts and too little skin.

29
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.320
What decides a cell's fate is how its signaling compares with that of the cells beside it.
